# deep learning model classifies an image into one of three categories: cat, dog, or bird. 
The actual class is represented by Y=[1,0,0], while the model predicts probabilities 
P=[0.7,0.2,0.1]. 
Write a Python program to calculate the cross-entropy loss between the actual class 
distribution and the predicted probabilities, and to compare the actual and predicted 
probabilities.




import numpy as np

Y = np.array([1,0,0])
P = np.array([0.7,0.2,0.1])
loss = -np.sum(Y*np.log(P))
print("Cross entropy:", loss)
